            <ArticleTitle>Acute paraplegia after myelography: decompensation of a herniatad thoracic disc.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>684-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02688690801911580</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 71-year-old patient presented with low back pain and slowly progressive weakness of both legs. Within a few hours after lumbar myelography, paraplegia below level L2 evolved. MR-imaging revealed a discogenic stenosis at level Th10/11. Immediate decompression by costo-transversectomy led to reversal of the neurological deficits.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
